      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Just north of downtown, the Tower District’s neon‑lit Art Deco theater opened in 1939 and still anchors the neighborhood’s shopping and nightlife.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitcalifornia.com/places-to-visit/fresno/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Fresno Grizzlies began play in 1998 as a Triple‑A Pacific Coast League team before moving to the California League in 2021.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fresno_Grizzlies",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Since 2002, the Grizzlies have called Chukchansi Park home, a downtown stadium that opened that year and replaced the old Pete Beiden Field.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fresno_Grizzlies",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Fresno State University’s Bulldogs enjoy one of the most passionate college followings in the country, with alumni like New York Yankee Aaron Judge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
